==============================================================================
AUDIT 2 -- RISK-FREE RATE CONSISTENCY
==============================================================================
research/metrics.py::sharpe(returns, bars_per_year) = mean(returns)/std(returns) * sqrt(bars_per_year)
No risk-free subtraction anywhere in the formula.
run_momentum_rotation.py calls the SAME function `sharpe()` for BOTH:
  - rotation configs: sharpe(net_ret, bars_per_year=BARS_PER_YEAR)   [driver line ~82]
  - SPY buy-and-hold: sharpe(ret, bars_per_year=BARS_PER_YEAR)       [spy_buy_hold(), line ~122]
CONSISTENT: both use raw (non-excess) returns, zero risk-free subtraction on both sides.
No fix needed; if a risk-free-adjusted Sharpe were desired it would need applying to BOTH
sides identically, which the current code already guarantees structurally (one function, two callers).

==============================================================================
AUDIT 3 -- TOTAL RETURN CORRECTNESS
==============================================================================
scripts/download_momentum_universe.py: ONE loop over UNIVERSE = SECTOR_ETFS + ASSET_ETFS + BENCHMARK
(BENCHMARK=['SPY'], ASSET_ETFS includes 'IEF'), single yf.download(..., auto_adjust=True) call site,
`close` column taken post-adjustment for every ticker with no branch -- SPY and IEF go through the
IDENTICAL code path as the ranked universe. Empirical confirmation (fresh pull, 2003-01 to 2003-06):
  SPY: adj/raw close ratio 2003-01-02=0.6515, 2003-05-30=0.6541 (ratio != 1 and DRIFTS toward 1 as of 2025 -- proves dividend/distribution reinvestment is baked into the adjusted series for BOTH the equity benchmark and the bond defensive leg).
  IEF: adj/raw close ratio 2003-01-02=0.5030, 2003-05-30=0.5095 (ratio != 1 and DRIFTS toward 1 as of 2025 -- proves dividend/distribution reinvestment is baked into the adjusted series for BOTH the equity benchmark and the bond defensive leg).

==============================================================================
AUDIT 4 -- SURVIVORSHIP
==============================================================================
The 17-ETF + SPY universe consists only of funds that exist and trade TODAY; any sector/asset-class
ETF that was ever delisted, merged, or never launched is absent by construction, and free data cannot
correct this -- stated as a known, unfixed limitation, not fabricated around.

